I had a brilliant gnomish wizard going. An early wand of wishing got me
the Eyes of the Overworld, +2 GDSM, and a magic marker (plus a couple
spare charges for pants-browning emergencies). Lucky polypiling got me
free action. Sacced for Magicbane and enchanted to +3. Other great
finds were "oR, BoH, cloak of displacement, jumping boots and various
nifty spellbooks (identify, cone of cold, haste self). My AC was -21 or
so (9 points of protection helped). I had amassed
sleep/fire/cold/poison resistance, telepathy, and teleportitis - which
went well with a =oTC. I must have eaten 8 or 9 tengus but no
intrinsic... wasn't fussed since I'd get it at XL17 anyway.

Did the quest. Dear oh dear, the Dark One really is a pushover. Even
without see invisible, he wasn't much more than a fly to be swatted.

Finally arrived at Medusa's island. Killed the titan before he had the
chance to summon anything more than a fire elemental. Took "oR off to
equip "EotA for telepathy in order to see the water creatures. Went
into medusa's chamber. "You meet Medusa's gaze. You turn to stone...
DYWYPI?" I couldn't believe it when I saw that! I was fully expecting
her to turn herself to stone right away, thanks to the "oR I wasn't
wearing.

This is the first time I've ever been killed by Medusa. I always
thought she was wimpy before. (Paradoxically, if you think she's wimpy,
you'll be too cavalier and she'll kill you; if you think she's
dangerous, there's no way she can hurt you.)



